    "title": "Rate-half distance-three calibrated conic kernel-lift normal form",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On the exact pair-Lagrange external design, scale each degree-2e complement H_x=P_Z/G_x by s_x=B(x)G_x(0). There are fixed degree-less-than-e polynomials R_0,R_1,R_2 such that s_xH_x=R_0+xR_1+x^2R_2+IJ_x with a unique degree-at-most-e kernel lift J_x whose leading coefficient is s_x. The R_j span the pair-quadratic rank, and the full family obeys product_x(R_0+xR_1+x^2R_2+IJ_x)=kappa P_Z^(4e+2). No low-rank or bounded-row-degree claim for the J_x is made.",
